{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-101643",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "First, we clear the rational expression by multiplying the equation through by $3$:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{2n-8}{3} & =-6(n+1) \\\\ 3\\cdot (\\frac{2n-8}{3}) & =3\\cdot (-6(n+1)) \\\\ \\cancel{3}\\cdot (\\frac{2n-8}{\\cancel{3}}) & =-18(n+1) \\\\ 2n-8 & =-18n-18\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we solve the remaining equation using the addition and multiplication principles:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2n-8 & =-18n-18 \\\\ 2n-8+18n & =-18n-18+18n \\\\ 20n-8 & =-18 \\\\ 20n-8+8 & =-18+8 \\\\ 20n & =-10 \\\\ \\frac{20n}{20} & =\\frac{-10}{20} \\\\ n & =-\\frac{10}{20} \\\\ n & =-\\frac{1}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
